#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# petersen_graph

#% text
# `petersen_graph()`: the Petersen graph, 10 vertices and 15 edges (an outer 5-cycle, an inner pentagram and five spokes).

#% text
# `petersen_graph(n, k)`: the generalized Petersen graph of 2n vertices: the outer n-cycle 1, ..., n, the spokes from i to n + i, and the inner edges from n + i to n + ((i + k) mod n), for 1 <= k < n. `petersen_graph(5, 2)` is the Petersen graph.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
petersen_graph()
#% output
#= image("petersen_graph.files/petersen_graph-1.svgz")

#% cell
edge_count(petersen_graph(8, 3))
#% output
#= 24

#% cell
petersen_graph(6, 1, vertex_size: 0)
#% output
#= image("petersen_graph.files/petersen_graph-3.svgz")

